a4632e6c2c4eb","inline:4301415542":"7ed336e62fbc22bd0c2fb5d8ccb6891d62b53a9b","review:5556199464":"7ed336e62fbc22bd0c2fb5d8ccb6891d62b53a9b","review:5556245192":"7ed336e62fbc22bd0c2fb5d8ccb6891d62b53a9b"},"parent":"f3054ae2fca167dda019488af98508351fb74068","patch_sha256":"94fcfe3b05aa6d6625012319bf87dffeeb2c38d882a3b3a192bc8981379f2a3b","tree":"0d0ca850f231b4de54c0a9809bea9cb2d374cd54"},"dispositions":{"findings":[{"analysis":"Both previously missed issues are addressed: commit 1 gates header capture in AbstractWrapperTest and InterceptorsTest and labels the header-enabled receive/experimental profiles with the exact builder selector; commit 2 restores experimental/header-enabled WrapperPropagationDisabledTest and WrapperSuppressReceiveSpansTest runs with receive telemetry left disabled, wired into check but neither labeled nor collected. The already-resolved synchronous-send and consumer-error coverage remains in the appropriate profiles, confirmed by exact JUnit discovery.","commit":2,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5556199464"},{"analysis":"The two open issues are fixed together across commits 1 and 2: the baseline now uses the empty default header selector, optional header capture is accurately labeled, and both wrapper regression subclasses have a separate experimental task outside metadata collection. Gradle task inspection and four separate broker-free fixture JVMs verify the configuration; discovery confirms both restored regression methods.","commit":2,"disposition":"fixed","key":"review:5556245192"},{"analysis":"Both fixtures now read test.captureMessagingHeaders, call setHeaders only when enabled, and use the same flag for their existing exact header assertions. testDefaultTelemetry leaves the flag and metadataConfig unset. The named receive and experimental profiles enable capture and include KafkaTelemetryBuilder.setHeaders(IncludeExclude.builder().setIncluded(\"Test-Message-*\").setExcluded(\"*-Excluded-Header\").build()) in their labels. Builder defaults and instrumentation-docs/readme.md explicitly establish that the synthetic-header exemption is javaagent-only. Runtime fixture probes confirm headers are absent by default and captured/excluded correctly when enabled.","commit":1,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4301415524"},{"analysis":"Added testExperimentalRegression selecting precisely the inherited testWrappers methods in WrapperPropagationDisabledTest and WrapperSuppressReceiveSpansTest. It enables experimental attributes and header capture, restoring the original true/true parameterized cases shown in the pre-PR AbstractWrapperTest, leaves receive telemetry at its false default, and is included in check with test classes/runtime classpath but no metadataConfig or collection-script entry. Gradle configuration assertions, test discovery, and broker-free fixture checks verify these settings.","commit":2,"disposition":"fixed","key":"inline:4301415542"}],"input_identity":{},"outcome":"fixes","request_digest":"adcc7d1e161f9fdcdc898b194d7b1f54cec207ac28f1c91239ae028d1d09f677","schema":2},"download_sha256":"6c08ffe254a5d010d3cb676927ba19d54824fee1b29bc10fef7aa47f67934e9f","frozen_sha":"f3054ae2fca167dda019488af98508351fb74068","pr":20645,"publication_eligible":false,"repo":"open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation","request_digest":"adcc7d1e161f9fdcdc898b194d7b1f54cec207ac28f1c91239ae028d1d09f677","request_id":"f5eb7c3cb7ae40bb925167aa83982544","run_attempt":1,"run_id":39004106371,"schema":2,"scope":"Structural/Git verification only. No target code or tests are executed.","server_artifact_digest":"sha256:6c08ffe254a5d010d3cb676927ba19d54824fee1b29bc10fef7aa47f67934e9f","verification":"verified","verification_run":{"attempt":1,"id":39005922316},"workflow_revision":"d24780fc2512e60cf9785c88eed4b4abd8a29158"},"request":{"authorized_actor_id":218610,"baseline_review_ids":[5549650212,5550204403,5550284665,5550407500,5555479981,5555559853,5555582689,5555798475,5555846501,5555892438,5555944763,5556199464,5556245192],"budgets":{"max_iterations":5,"propagation_seconds":120,"retention_days":14,"worker_timeout_minutes":30},"commit_author":{"id":218610,"login":"trask"},"findings":[{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nExperimental wrapper regression coverage is reduced, and header capture remains inconsistent with the profile labels.\n\n**No open issues** \ud83c\udf89\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>2 previously missed issues</strong></summary>\n\nIn code that hasn't changed since last review\n\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Restore experimental-attribute wrapper test coverage</summary>\n\n`instrumentation/\u200bkafka/\u200bkafka-clients/\u200bkafka-clients-2.6/\u200blibrary/\u200bbuild.gradle.kts:89`\n\n[Testing] Replacing the shared wrapper parameterization removes the experimental-attribute runs of `WrapperPropagationDisabledTest` and `WrapperSuppressReceiveSpansTest`. The only task enabling `test.captureExperimentalSpanAttributes` now excludes both classes, leaving their bootstrap-server and queue-time assertions unexercised. Restore these runs in a separate task wired into `check`, without adding it to collection or giving it a metadata label. Leave receive telemetry disabled there to preserve their previous configuration.\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/low-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Low severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> Gate header capture and label opt-in profile correctly</summary>\n\n`instrumentation/\u200bkafka/\u200bkafka-clients/\u200bkafka-clients-2.6/\u200blibrary/\u200bbuild.gradle.kts:31`\n\n[Testing] Both successful-operation fixtures selected here unconditionally call `setHeaders(...)` (`InterceptorsTest:21` and `AbstractWrapperTest:79`), although the builder default captures no headers. This labels a header-enabled library profile as `when: default`, and the optional profiles omit that builder setting too. `instrumentation-docs/readme.md:41\u201347` exempts only shared javaagent header capture. Gate capture in both fixtures, keep it off for the default profile, and preserve header-enabled coverage in a named opt-in profile labeled with its `KafkaTelemetryBuilder.setHeaders(...)` configuration.\n</details>\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>2 resolved since last review</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Include testConsumerError in receive telemetry profile](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20645#discussion_r4301209550)\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Retain synchronous producer send failure test](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20645#discussion_r4301209507)\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5556199464","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5556199464},{"body":"<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udfe1 Changes recommended\n\nBaseline header capture remains enabled, and experimental coverage is lost for two wrapper regression tests.\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>2 open issues</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Gate header capture and label header-enabled profiles correctly](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20645#discussion_r4301415524) \u00b7 New\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/medium-v2-light.png\" alt=\"Medium severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [Restore experimental-attribute regression coverage for wrapper tests](https://github.com/open-telemetry/opentelemetry-java-instrumentation/pull/20645#discussion_r4301415542) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>","comment_id":null,"key":"review:5556245192","kind":"body","line":null,"path":null,"review_id":5556245192},{"body":"[Testing] Both successful-operation fixtures selected here unconditionally call `KafkaTelemetryBuilder.setHeaders(...)`, so `testDefaultTelemetry` records header-enabled telemetry under `default`, although the builder default captures no headers. The receive and experimental profiles also omit this applied setting from their labels. This leaves #20546's library profile separation incomplete; the shared synthetic-header exception applies only to javaagent fixtures. Gate capture and its expectations in both `AbstractWrapperTest` and `InterceptorsTest`, leave it off for the baseline, and label header-enabled profiles with the actual builder configuration.","comment_commit_id":"f3054ae2fca167dda019488af98508351fb74068","comment_id":4301415524,"key":"inline:4301415524","kind":"inline","line":31,"original_commit_id":"f3054ae2fca167dda019488af98508351fb74068","original_line":31,"path":"instrumentation/kafka/kafka-clients/kafka-clients-2.6/library/build.gradle.kts","review_commit_id":"f3054ae2fca167dda019488af98508351fb74068","review_id":5556245192,"review_submitted_at":"2026-10-17T04:41:08Z","root_author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"thread_context":[{"author":{"id":175728472,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCnlnWA","type":"Bot"},"body_hash":"3f96c9471b5acd450f1eaffd984a1a73b47c482004d297b0ca7c3f62c0c0ad9b","id":4301415524,"parent":null,"updated_at":"2026-10-17T04:41:08Z"}],"thread_id":"PRRT_kwDODJKVX86tdJQL"},{"body":"[Testing] Replacing the inherited parameterized test with a JVM flag removes the experimental-attribute cases for